From 6af2b61edd886dd5dd5b6c7c9cfadb533c673123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:39:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] incusd: Refuse access to the volumes holding the daemon's
 data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The storage.*_volume custom volumes hold every project's backups,
images and logs but were only guarded on rename, snapshot and delete,
so a client restricted to the default project could export, read,
write, rebuild, attach or migrate them.

This addresses GHSA-8m9x-vx2q-7f9q (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit da3801e0f5d246bc19a1022312701c14848f216f)
